Invalidation: support generation redoes the lift detection.

OrcaSlicer 2.5's version of patches/snapmaker/0012. PrintObject::detect_overhangs_for_lift
fills each layer's loverhangs after support generation, and support generation (its
overhang detection, also run to check whether supports are needed) clears them.
Invalidating posSupportMaterial (a speed, a brim, a move) left posDetectOverhangsForLift
done, so a Print sliced again (desktop does after such a change; the browser engine keeps
the last slice's Print) lost every overhang and lifted differently from a fresh slice.
2.5 already redoes it on a new layer height (posSlice); this adds posSupportMaterial.

--- a/src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/PrintObject.cpp
@@ -1899,7 +1899,9 @@
         // The exact belt_floor_z_shift is recomputed when slice() runs again.
         m_belt_floor_z_shift_cache_valid = false;
     } else if (step == posSupportMaterial) {
-        invalidated |= this->invalidate_steps({ posSimplifySupportPath });
+        // cloud-slicer: support generation clears each layer's overhangs, which
+        // the lift detection fills in after it, so it has to run again too.
+        invalidated |= this->invalidate_steps({ posSimplifySupportPath, posDetectOverhangsForLift });
         invalidated |= m_print->invalidate_steps({ psSkirtBrim });
         // SlicingParameters depend on support config (enable_support /
         // raft_layers / enforce_support_layers feed min/max layer height in
